@page "/docs/primitives/combobox"

<DocsPage Title="Combobox" Description="An input combined with a list of predefined items to select.">
    <ComponentPreview Name="primitives/combobox-hero" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Usage guidelines" />
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Combobox is a filterable Select:</strong> Use Combobox when the input is restricted to a set of predefined items, like <a href="/docs/primitives/select">Select</a>, but whose items can be filtered by typing. Prefer it over Select when there are enough items to warrant filtering.</li>
        <li><strong>Avoid for simple search widgets:</strong> Combobox doesn't allow free-form text. For search widgets, consider <a href="/docs/primitives/autocomplete">Autocomplete</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Avoid when not rendering an input:</strong> Use <a href="/docs/primitives/select">Select</a> instead if no input is rendered: it includes accessibility features specific to a listbox without an input.</li>
        <li><strong>Form controls must have an accessible name:</strong> If <code>ComboboxInput</code> is the form control, label it with a native <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> or <code>FieldLabel</code>, or give it an <code>aria-label</code> when no visible label is rendered. <code>ComboboxLabel</code> labels <code>ComboboxTrigger</code>, for the pattern where the input is inside the popup and the trigger is the form control.</li>
        <li><strong>Closing animations:</strong> The popup stays rendered until its closing animation finishes. See <a href="/docs/primitives/animation">Animation</a>.</li>
    </ul>
